## Context

Ticket 1451 (PR #2225, merged) folded the per-project SMELT.md into the
smelt skill. Its raid reported leftovers, recorded in its journal entry and
in the PR #2226 wrap-up, with no ticket. The author asked (2026-11-07) to pass
them to the harness.

## Work

1. Review record of PR #2225 lacks the writer attribution line: add it.
2. `tests/test_smelt_migrate.py`: fast-tier tests now spawn git without the
   integration marker; mark or restructure them.
3. `scripts/smelt_migrate.py:316`: recovery hint prints `HEAD:<name>`; it
   must be `HEAD:./<name>` (wrong when the project is a repo subdirectory).
4. `scripts/memory_sizes.py`: no test for a topic filename with a space.
5. Re-running the migration after a prompt is retired no longer lists files
   still citing the retired prompt; restore that listing or state why not.
6. Apply the author's 2026-11-07 decision on Commission pinned rulings:
   replace `memory/topics/commission.md` with the approved text at
   `/home/haduong/.claude/jobs/9d9691f0/tmp/commission.approved.md`
   (drafted from origin/main 5284fde; 37 pins -> 18; every kept pin's
   original wording verified verbatim, context appended as "Scope:" sentences;
   retired pins listed under Retired with their carrier). If commission.md
   changed on origin/main since 5284fde, merge rather than overwrite and say
   so. Do not reword the approved pins.

Severity: below the ticket floor individually; bundled as one handoff at the
author's request. Fix inline where trivial.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Items 1–5 fixed or each dismissed with a one-line reason in the log
- [ ] Item 6: commission.md matches the approved text (or a stated merge of it); guide bytes reported by scripts/memory_sizes.py
- [ ] Harness gate passes
